# Q: is any unit left stalled — waiting for a route it is never going to get?
#
#   MiVic.Game.exe --probe tools/probe/stall.probe --probe-out artifacts/probe/stall.txt
#
# The default skirmish, unmodified, six hundred ticks of it, with the client's own wander orders
# running: this is the match the bug was measured in. Nothing here places anything or orders
# anything — the script only watches.
#
# What was wrong: an attack order sets a move goal at the target's position, and the route search
# clips a goal the mover cannot enter to the nearest cell it can. The goal itself was left where it
# was ordered, so the arrival test and the route answered about two different places — the unit
# walked to the clipped cell, never arrived at the ordered one, asked for the route again the next
# tick, was told by the route search that it was already in the goal cell and *succeeded*, which
# cleared PathFailures, and did that forever. The reading is `path 0 cells at 0, waiting for a
# route, 0 failures` with travel frozen and nothing anywhere reporting a fault, because nothing was
# failing.
#
# `routes` is the command that counts it and the check it records, so a run of this script fails
# while any unit is in that state. `unit` is the same reading for one unit at a time: slot 259 is a
# unit this was measured on, and the second reading of it is four hundred ticks later, which is what
# turns "it is waiting" into "it is still waiting".

# --- six hundred ticks of the standard match ------------------------------------------------------
tick 600

# --- one unit, in full ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Before: `move goal (x 40.3, z 147.1) m, 205.1 m to go, path 0 cells at 0, waiting for a route,
# 0 failures` and an explicit attack order on a Δυτικοί Γραφείο Σχεδιασμού 205 m away. After: the
# move order is gone because it was carried out — the same unit is standing in weapon range of the
# building it was sent at.
unit 259

# --- the whole map ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# One line per unit waiting for a route *with a move goal*, which is the stalled state, plus the
# longest any unit has waited since the script started and the check that guards it.
routes

# --- four hundred ticks later -------------------------------------------------------------------
# The line that made this a bug rather than a slow start: a stalled unit is still stalled later, and
# a queued one has been served.
tick 400
unit 259
routes

# --- the measurements ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately no `expect` lines for the two counts: `expect` compares two literals and never reads
# the world, so `expect "units stalled" 0 0` would pass on the day it was wrong. The count is a check
# `routes` records for itself, and the run fails when it does not hold. The counting test in
# MiVic.Core.Tests asks the same question of the same match on the same seed and tick
# (UnreachableGoalTests.TheStandardSkirmishLeavesNoUnitWaitingForARoute), where the answer before the
# fix was 200 — 116 of them over a hundred consecutive ticks, and 40 that never moved a millimetre in
# six hundred.
